use std
into envmap.amni

Namespace envmap; imports gfx, os, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.codec_hdr. Image-based lighting: a cube map whose mip levels hold the environment prefiltered for GGX roughness and, in the last level, for a cosine lobe. Module vars: `on` bool false, `physical` bool false, `intensity` f32 1.0, `rotation` f32 0.0 (radians about +y), `blur` f32 0.0 (the roughness the background is drawn at), `size` int 512, `samples` int 512, `irr_samples` int 2048, `cube` gfx::Texture, `dummy` gfx::Texture, `smp` gfx::Sampler, `smp_wrap` gfx::Sampler, `pipe_equi` gfx::Pipeline, `pipe_ggx` gfx::Pipeline, `ready` bool false, `lv` int 0. Struct `EnvU { p float4 }`.

`setup()` does nothing when `ready`. It builds `pipe_equi` from `embed_shader("shaders/screen.vert")` and `embed_shader("shaders/env_equi.frag")`, `pipe_ggx` from screen.vert and `embed_shader("shaders/env_ggx.frag")`, `smp = gfx::sampler(gfx::LINEAR, gfx::CLAMP)`, `smp_wrap = gfx::sampler(gfx::SamplerDesc { min_filter: gfx::LINEAR, mag_filter: gfx::LINEAR, mip_filter: gfx::LINEAR, wrap_u: gfx::REPEAT, wrap_v: gfx::CLAMP, wrap_w: gfx::CLAMP })`, and `dummy = gfx::texture(gfx::TextureDesc { kind: gfx::TEXTURE_CUBE, format: gfx::RGBA8, usage: gfx::SAMPLED, width: 1, height: 1 })`, uploading 4 zero bytes to each of its 6 layers with `gfx::update_texture(dummy, gfx::Region { layer: f as i32, w: 1, h: 1, d: 1 }, bytes)`. Then `ready = true`.

`levels(s int) int` counts mip levels from s halving down to 16 inclusive (s = 512 gives 6), at least 2.

`faces(t gfx::Texture, m int, p gfx::Pipeline, src gfx::Texture, s gfx::Sampler, rough f32, count f32, src_size f32)` runs one pass per face f in 0..6 with `gfx::begin_pass(gfx::PassDesc { color: [t, gfx::Texture { 0 }, gfx::Texture { 0 }, gfx::Texture { 0 }], layer: f as i32, mip: m as i32, .. })` (skip the face when it fails, using guard), then `gfx::bind(p)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::FRAGMENT, 0, src, s)`, `gfx::uniforms(gfx::FRAGMENT, 0, EnvU { p: float4 { f as f32, rough, count, src_size } })`, `gfx::draw(3)`, `gfx::end_pass()`.

`filter(raw gfx::Texture, n int)` prefilters the fully mipped source cube `raw` of face size n into `cube`. When `cube.id` is 0 or `lv` differs from `levels(n)`, free the old cube with `gfx::release` if it exists and make a new one: kind gfx::TEXTURE_CUBE, gfx::RGBA16F, usage gfx::SAMPLED | gfx::COLOR_TARGET, width and height `n as i32`, mips `levels(n) as i32`; set `lv`. For each level m in 0..lv: the last level uses rough -1.0 and `irr_samples` samples; level 0 uses rough 0.0; the others use rough `m as f32 / (lv - 2) as f32` and `samples` samples. Call `faces(cube, m, pipe_ggx, raw, smp, rough, count, n as f32)`.

`sun_color(to_sun float3, power f32, haze f32) float3` returns the sun light that reaches 0.2 km above the ground, as `power` times the transmittance along the unit vector to_sun. With o = (0, 6360.2) in the plane (horizontal = sqrt(1 - to_sun.y^2), vertical = to_sun.y), it returns zero when the ray hits the sphere of radius 6360 before leaving (b = o.y * to_sun.y, c = 6360.2^2 - 6360^2, b < 0 and b^2 > c). Otherwise it walks 64 equal steps from o to the sphere of radius 6460 (far distance -b + sqrt(b^2 - (6360.2^2 - 6460^2))), summing at each step midpoint, with h = distance from the origin - 6360: `r = exp(-h / 8)`, `m = haze * exp(-h / 1.2)`, `z = max(1 - abs(h - 25) / 15, 0)`, optical depth in red `5.802e-3 * r + 4.44e-3 * m + 0.650e-3 * z`, green `13.558e-3 * r + 4.44e-3 * m + 1.881e-3 * z`, blue `33.1e-3 * r + 4.44e-3 * m + 0.085e-3 * z`, each times the step length. Each channel of the result is `power * exp(-depth)`. Work in `real`.

`set_sky(to_sun float3, power f32, haze f32, clouds f32, n int, wind_x f32, wind_z f32)` calls `setup()`, then fills the environment from a simulated atmosphere. It makes `ms`, a 32 by 32 RGBA16F SAMPLED | COLOR_TARGET 2D texture, and draws it in one pass with `pipe_ms` (bound with `gfx::bind`, three vertices via `gfx::draw(3)`), fragment uniform slot 0 being `EnvU { p: float4 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.18, haze } }`. It makes `raw`, an n by n RGBA16F cube with SAMPLED | COLOR_TARGET usage and the same mip count as `set_equirect` computes from n. For each face f in 0..6 it runs a pass on `raw` with `layer: f as i32` that binds `pipe_sky`, binds `ms` to fragment texture slot 0 with `smp`, pushes `EnvSkyU { p: float4 { f as f32, 0.2, 0.18, haze }, sun: float4 { to_sun.x, to_sun.y, to_sun.z, power }, cloud: float4 { clouds, wind_x, wind_z, 0.0 } }` at fragment uniform slot 0, and draws three vertices. Then `gfx::generate_mips(raw)`, `filter(raw, n)`, releases `ms` and `raw`, and sets `on = true` and `physical = true`. `struct EnvSkyU { p float4, sun float4, cloud float4 }`. `setup` also builds `pipe_ms` from screen.vert and `embed_shader("shaders/env_ms.frag")`, and `pipe_sky` from screen.vert and `embed_shader("shaders/env_sky.frag")`.

`set_equirect(rgba const f32[:], w int, h int)` calls setup, converts with `codec_hdr::half_pixels` into a local byte array, makes a `gfx::RGBA16F` sampled 2D texture with `width: w as i32, height: h as i32`, uploads with `gfx::update_texture(t, bytes[..])`, makes a raw cube (kind gfx::TEXTURE_CUBE, gfx::RGBA16F, usage gfx::SAMPLED | gfx::COLOR_TARGET, width and height `size as i32`, mips (as i32) = 1 + floor(log2(size)) counted by halving), calls `faces(raw, 0, pipe_equi, t, smp_wrap, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0)`, `gfx::generate_mips(raw)`, `filter(raw, size)`, frees t and raw with `gfx::release`, and sets `on = true`. It also sets `physical = false`.

`load(path const byte[:]) bool` reads the file with `read_file` into a local byte array (false on failure), decodes with `codec_hdr::decode` into a local f32 array (false when not ok), calls `set_equirect` and returns true.

`texture() gfx::Texture` returns `cube` when `on` and `cube.id != 0`, otherwise `dummy`; it calls `setup()` first.

`spec_lod() f32` returns `(lv - 2) as f32` and `irr_lod() f32` returns `(lv - 1) as f32`.
